[{:db/id -1, :doc/id "doc-adr-2605262500-pr-prep-260527", :doc/title "ADR-2605262500 PR Prep — branch strategy + cross-ADR drift + PR draft (cycle 45)", :doc/status "active", :doc/doc_type "how-to", :doc/source-format "edn", :doc/body "\n# ADR-2605262500 PR Prep — cycle 45 (2026-05-27)\n\nThree deliverables for the PR readiness gate:\n\n1. **Branch scope strategy** — concrete options for the 379-commit branch\n2. **Cross-ADR drift outreach checklist** — per-ADR owner notes for 12 orphan entries\n3. **PR description draft** — reviewer-facing PR template (paste-ready)\n\n## Part 1 — Branch scope strategy\n\n### Branch state (2026-05-27 measurement)\n\n| Metric | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Branch | `feat/yakushi-wave-1c-r1-commissioning` |\n| Commits ahead of `main` | **379** |\n| Commits touching ADR-2605262500 paths | **26** |\n| Commits with explicit `adr-2605262500` in message | 1 (cycle 44) |\n| ADRs represented on the branch (sampling) | yakushi 1c / kusawake / ADR-2605261600 e7m-sim / ADR-2605261800 kami-engine / ADR-2605262100 moemoekyun R1 / ADR-2605262200 charter amendment / ADR-2605262300 R2 train arch / ADR-2605262400 corpus assembler / **ADR-2605262500 (this work)** / 多数の Tier-B R0 wave / Charter Preamble / Land Trust Wave 2 |\n\nThe branch name suggests yakushi was the origin point, but ~10+ ADRs accumulated work here in parallel agent sessions. **It is not natively an ADR-2605262500 branch.**\n\n### Three options\n\n#### Option A — Cherry-pick to focused branch (RECOMMENDED)\n\nCreate new branch from `main`, cherry-pick the 26 ADR-2605262500-scope commits.\n\n**Pros**:\n- Reviewable scope (~26 commits, ~3.5k LOC delta)\n- Clear ADR alignment (every commit traces to ADR-2605262500)\n- Ships ADR-2605262500 cleanly without waiting for other ADRs\n- Easy to add ADR-2605262500-only CI gates\n\n**Cons**:\n- Mixed-content \"wave\" commits (`chore(wave): …`) will pull in non-ADR-2605262500 files; would need partial cherry-pick or commit splitting\n- 5 commits are \"mixed wave\" (`918e7df5f`, `4845d1704`, `67d2d5a0e`, `28d32f061`, `43351b5c2`); each needs surgery\n- Original commit dates lost (cherry-pick replays as today's date unless `-x` + commit hooks negotiated)\n\n**Estimated effort**: 2-3 hours of git surgery.\n\n**Concrete command sequence** (DO NOT run without user authorization):\n```bash\ngit checkout main\ngit pull origin main\ngit checkout -b feat/adr-2605262500-robotics-world-data-pipeline\n\n# Clean cherry-picks (single-ADR commits):\ngit cherry-pick -x a77fda125 0dc1f9b16 5485234d8 3ee2e7d7f\ngit cherry-pick -x ed724c3c9 713d66e02 fdf92ba33 a9fcf88d6\n# … (~21 more)\n\n# Mixed wave commits require partial cherry-pick:\ngit cherry-pick --no-commit 918e7df5f\ngit reset HEAD -- <non-ADR-2605262500 paths>\ngit checkout -- <non-ADR-2605262500 paths>\ngit commit -m \"feat(adr-2605262500): wave subset — robotics world data\"\n```\n\n#### Option B — Push entire branch as bundle PR\n\nPush `feat/yakushi-wave-1c-r1-commissioning` as one PR.\n\n**Pros**:\n- Zero git surgery\n- Preserves full commit history + dates\n\n**Cons**:\n- 379 commits is **unreviewable** in practice\n- Reviewer would have no way to scope-check\n- ADR-2605262500 scope buried in noise\n\n**Not recommended.**\n\n#### Option C — Squash-rebuild\n\nCreate new branch from main, copy current state of ADR-2605262500-owned files (the working-tree snapshot), commit as one or a few logical squashed commits.\n\n**Pros**:\n- Easiest git operation (no cherry-pick conflicts)\n- Reviewer sees clean diff vs main\n- Can structure as W0 / W1 / W2 / W3 / W4 wave commits\n\n**Cons**:\n- Loses commit history detail (44 cycles collapsed)\n- Loses \"this fix happened because of that observation\" causality\n- Implementation retrospective doc partially mitigates this\n\n**Estimated effort**: 30 minutes.\n\n**Concrete command sequence**:\n```bash\ngit checkout main\ngit pull origin main\ngit checkout -b feat/adr-2605262500-robotics-world-data-pipeline\n\n# Copy ADR-2605262500-owned files from feat/yakushi-wave-1c-r1-commissioning\nfor path in <list of ADR-2605262500 paths>; do\n  git checkout feat/yakushi-wave-1c-r1-commissioning -- \"$path\"\ndone\n\n# Stage + commit as wave subsets:\ngit add 90-docs/adr/2605262500-*.md && git commit -m \"feat(adr-2605262500): W0 — ADR + retrospective\"\ngit add 70-tools/e7m-dataset/src/e7m_dataset/fetchers/ && git commit -m \"feat(adr-2605262500): W1 — Tier-A + Tier-C fetchers\"\ngit add 70-tools/e7m-sim/scripts/assemble*.py 70-tools/e7m-sim/scenes/ && git commit -m \"feat(adr-2605262500): W2 — USD assembler + 9 scenes\"\ngit add 70-tools/e7m-dataset/src/e7m_dataset/vision_pii*.py 70-tools/e7m-dataset/tests/test_vision_pii*.py && git commit -m \"feat(adr-2605262500): W3 — Vision PII filter (3 ONNX backends)\"\ngit add 70-tools/e7m-sim/scripts/eval_sim_metrics.py && git commit -m \"feat(adr-2605262500): W4 — G11 quality gate eval CLI\"\ngit add 70-tools/scripts/lint/ 70-tools/scripts/diagnose/ lefthook.yml .github/workflows/deps-toml-paths.yml && git commit -m \"feat(adr-2605262500): operator UX + book-keeping enforcement\"\ngit add 90-docs/baien/adr-2605262500-* deps.toml && git commit -m \"docs(adr-2605262500): retrospective + runbook + smoke + deps.toml\"\n```\n\n### Recommendation\n\n**Option C (squash-rebuild) is the pragmatic best.**\n\nRationale:\n- The 44-cycle implementation history is **already preserved** in\n  `adr-2605262500-implementation-retrospective-260527.md` (39-cycle chronology)\n  + `adr-2605262500-runbook-smoke-260527.md` (cycle 44 evidence).\n- Reviewers care more about \"does the end state work\" than \"what was\n  the 7th iteration's debugging trail.\"\n- Option A's git surgery has surface area for mistakes (the cycle 43\n  re-commit incident is a real example).\n- Option C cleanly maps to W0..W4 ADR wave structure, which is how\n  the ADR itself is organized.\n\n**Decision required from user before any branch action.**\n\n## Part 2 — Cross-ADR drift cleanup outreach\n\n### Full-repo verifier output (2026-05-27 cycle 45)\n\n`python3 70-tools/scripts/lint/verify_deps_toml_paths.py`\n\n```\ndeps.toml path audit: 571/586 entries resolve\nMISSING (15):\n  [adrs] 90-docs/adr/2605250730-tatekata-construction-r1-benchtop-poc.edn (reserved)  (2605250730)\n  [adrs] 90-docs/adr/2605250745-tatekata-construction-r2-pilot-site.edn (reserved)  (2605250745)\n  [adrs] 90-docs/adr/2605250760-tatekata-construction-r3-community-scale.edn (reserved)  (2605250760)\n  [modules] 00-contracts/lexicons/com/etzhayyim/apps/unispsc  (['2605180900'])\n  [modules] 00-contracts/lexicons/com/etzhayyim/apps/isic  (['2605180900'])\n  [modules] 40-engine/kotoba/crates/kotoba-kotodama/py/src/kotodama/langserver  (['2605180900'])\n  [modules] 50-infra/k8s/lg-open-isic  (['2605180900'])\n  [modules] 60-apps/etzhayyim-cell-fleet-dashboard  (['2605192415'])\n  [modules] 40-engine/kotoba/crates/kotoba-kotodama/py/src/kotodama/mmsheaf  (['2605250700', '2605092345', '2605092350', '2605101000', '2605231400', '2605231500', '2605241900', '2605215000', '2605192200'])\n  [modules] 40-engine/kotoba/crates/kotoba-kotodama/cells/mmsheaf_diffusion_aggregator  (['2605250700', '2605231902', '2605231500', '2605242545', '2605241900'])\n  [modules] 70-tools/isaac-lab-task-port  (['2605261600'])\n  [modules] 90-docs/baien/moemoekyun-r1.4-corpus-manifest.jsonl  (ADR-2605262100)\n  [modules] 90-docs/baien/moemoekyun-r1.4-eval.jsonl  (ADR-2605262100)\n  [modules] 90-docs/baien/moemoekyun-models.jsonl  (ADR-2605262100)\n  [modules] 70-tools/baien-moemoekyun-train/recipes/seed-blocks/  (ADR-2605262400)\n```\n\n### Categorization\n\n#### Category A — Accepted reservations (no action needed)\n\n| Entry | ADR | Why accepted |\n|---|---|---|\n| `…2605250730-tatekata-construction-r1-benchtop-poc.md (reserved)` | 2605250730 | tatekata R1 ADR not yet authored; \"(reserved)\" marker explicit |\n| `…2605250745-tatekata-construction-r2-pilot-site.md (reserved)` | 2605250745 | R2 ADR not yet authored |\n| `…2605250760-tatekata-construction-r3-community-scale.md (reserved)` | 2605250760 | R3 ADR not yet authored |\n\nThese are placeholder reservations that the verifier currently flags\nas MISSING but are intentional. **Suggested fix**: enhance verifier to\nrecognize `(reserved)` suffix as accepted state, then count these as\n**571 resolve + 3 reserved + 12 drift = 586** for clarity.\n\n#### Category B — ADR-2605180900 etzhayyim→etzhayyim rename remnants (4 paths)\n\n| Path | Status | Owner |\n|---|---|---|\n| `00-contracts/lexicons/com/etzhayyim/apps/unispsc` | etzhayyim→etzhayyim rename incomplete | ADR-2605180900 author |\n| `00-contracts/lexicons/com/etzhayyim/apps/isic` | etzhayyim→etzhayyim rename incomplete | ADR-2605180900 author |\n| `40-engine/kotoba/crates/kotoba-kotodama/py/src/kotodama/langserver` | etzhayyim→etzhayyim rename incomplete | ADR-2605180900 author |\n| `50-infra/k8s/lg-open-isic` | renamed elsewhere? | ADR-2605180900 author |\n\n**Context** (from CLAUDE.md root §\"Do Not\"):\n> Do not rename `etzhayyim-*` identifiers in `50-infra/cluster/murakumo/` or\n> `40-engine/kotoba/crates/kotoba-kotodama/py/` outside the Step 8 cutover wave. Per\n> ADR-2605214000 §3 + ADR-2605215000 §4, the renames are itemised in\n> `MIGRATION-NOTES.md` files and must execute as one atomic PR after\n> legal registration.\n\nSo these 4 are **intentional pre-cutover state**. The deps.toml entries\nwere added optimistically expecting the cutover to happen. **Suggested\naction**: Either (a) remove the deps.toml entries until the rename\nlands, or (b) mark them `(deferred-rename)` similar to `(reserved)`.\n\n**Outreach target**: ADR-2605180900 / 2605214000 / 2605215000 owner.\n\n#### Category C — ADR-2605192415 etzhayyim-cell-fleet-dashboard (1 path)\n\n| Path | Status |\n|---|---|\n| `60-apps/etzhayyim-cell-fleet-dashboard` | Listed in CLAUDE.md religious-corp wave (`Status` row 13) but no impl |\n\n**Context**: ADR-2605192415 is \"religious-corp daemon architecture\";\nthe cell-fleet-dashboard was a planned 60-apps module that hasn't been\nscaffolded. **Suggested action**: Mark `(reserved)` in deps.toml, or\nremove the entry until the dashboard is built.\n\n**Outreach target**: ADR-2605192415 owner (likely you, jun@).\n\n#### Category D — mmsheaf paths (2 paths, multi-ADR-referenced)\n\n| Path | Referenced by |\n|---|---|\n| `40-engine/kotoba/crates/kotoba-kotodama/py/src/kotodama/mmsheaf` | ADR-2605250700 + 8 others |\n| `40-engine/kotoba/crates/kotoba-kotodama/cells/mmsheaf_diffusion_aggregator` | ADR-2605250700 + 4 others |\n\n**Context**: `mmsheaf_diffusion_aggregator` is a planned cell from the\nADR-2605250700 wave that hasn't been written. Many ADRs reference it as\na dependency. **Suggested action**: Same — mark `(reserved)`.\n\n**Outreach target**: ADR-2605250700 owner. NOTE: 9 ADRs reference this\npath; the entry has very high \"drift-blast-radius\" — fixing it\nunblocks many downstream books.\n\n#### Category E — ADR-2605261600 isaac-lab-task-port (1 path) **[OUR NEIGHBOR]**\n\n| Path | Status |\n|---|---|\n| `70-tools/isaac-lab-task-port` | Reserved in ADR-2605261600 e7m-sim charter; not yet scaffolded |\n\n**Context**: This is in ADR-2605262500's sibling territory. The\nADR-2605261600 e7m-sim charter explicitly reserves this path as the\nsole runtime carve-out for Isaac Lab Apache-2.0 task DSL header port.\n**Suggested action**: Mark `(reserved)` — same pattern as tatekata\nR1/R2/R3.\n\n**Outreach target**: ADR-2605261600 owner.\n\n#### Category F — ADR-2605262100/262400 moemoekyun corpus paths (4 paths)\n\n| Path | Status |\n|---|---|\n| `90-docs/baien/moemoekyun-r1.4-corpus-manifest.jsonl` | R1.4 in-flight; manifest will appear when training starts |\n| `90-docs/baien/moemoekyun-r1.4-eval.jsonl` | R1.4 in-flight |\n| `90-docs/baien/moemoekyun-models.jsonl` | R1+ output registry |\n| `70-tools/baien-moemoekyun-train/recipes/seed-blocks/` | R0 paths-reserved; impl pending |\n\n**Context**: ADR-2605262100 R1 sub-charter says \"first runnable code\nlands at R1.0 probe\" — these files will be created naturally as the\ntraining pipeline starts producing artifacts. **Suggested action**:\nMark all 4 `(reserved-until-R1)` or remove until first artifact lands.\n\n**Outreach target**: ADR-2605262100 / 2605262400 (likely you).\n\n### Outreach message template (reusable)\n\nFor ADRs with non-yourself owners (in this repo essentially all ADRs\nare authored by `jun@`, so the \"outreach\" is internal scheduling):\n\n```\nSubject: deps.toml drift — ADR-XXXXXXXXX paths\n\nHi <owner>,\n\nThe repo-wide deps.toml path verifier flagged the following paths as\nMISSING in ADR-XXXXXXXXX's [[modules]] entries:\n\n  - <path 1>\n  - <path 2>\n\nThese can be resolved by either:\n  (a) Adding the placeholder dir/file (if the impl is in-flight)\n  (b) Marking with `(reserved)` suffix (if intentionally future-dated)\n  (c) Removing the entry (if the path was speculative)\n\nSuggested action: <one of a/b/c per path>\n\nOnce landed, the full-repo verifier exits with 586/586 clean.\n\nADR-2605262500 cycle 45 audit (2026-05-27)\n```\n\n### Recommended cleanup wave\n\nIf the user owns most/all ADRs (which appears to be the case here),\nbatch them into one cleanup commit on a separate branch:\n\n```bash\ngit checkout main\ngit checkout -b chore/deps-toml-drift-cleanup-260527\n# Edit deps.toml to add (reserved) suffix or remove orphan [[modules]] entries\ngit commit -m \"chore(deps): mark 12 orphan paths as (reserved) — full-repo verifier 586/586 clean\"\n```\n\nThis is **separate from the ADR-2605262500 PR** and should ship first\nto give the ADR-2605262500 PR a clean book-keeping baseline.\n\n## Part 3 — ADR-2605262500 PR description draft\n\nThe PR description below is **paste-ready**. Use with whichever branch\nstrategy from Part 1 is chosen.\n\n---\n\n```markdown\n# ADR-2605262500 — Robotics-sim world-data ingestion + kami-usd pipeline\n\nImplements ADR-2605262500 (the geospatial-3D axis sibling of\nADR-2605262400 organism-perception axis). 44 implementation cycles via\nself-paced `/loop`; full chronology in\n`90-docs/baien/adr-2605262500-implementation-retrospective-260527.edn`.\n\n## Summary\n\n- **W0** — ADR + 4-doc dossier (charter / retrospective / runbook / smoke evidence)\n- **W1** — 8 fetchers: Sentinel-2 / SRTM / Overture / MS-Buildings / USGS 3DEP / OpenUSD samples / HF 3D NC / Mapillary\n- **W2** — USD scene assembler (9 R1 scenes for wadachi / suki / sarutahiko / igata / futawa / tatekata / hodoki / tsutae / makura) + W2.4 rasterio integration with defensive Pillow fallback\n- **W3** — Vision PII filter (3 ONNX backends: CenterFace / yolov8-face / RetinaFace) + auto-detect kind classifier + child-fail-closed G5 invariant\n- **W4** — G11 quality gate eval CLI (PSNR/SSIM/Chamfer/IoU composite ≥ 0.75)\n- **Operator UX** — 3 diagnostic CLIs (`vision_pii_diagnose` / `pds_diagnose` / `assemble_diagnose`) + unified `e7m_preflight.py` (4-in-1 readiness check)\n- **Book-keeping enforcement** — `verify_deps_toml_paths.py` CLI + lefthook hook + GitHub Actions workflow (PR gate + nightly baseline tracker)\n\n## Constitutional invariants enforced\n\nAll from ADR-2605262500 §\"Gates\" — these CANNOT be amended without\nCouncil Lv6+ ≥3:\n\n- **G2** Vision PII filter MANDATORY for Mapillary fetch\n- **G4** Tier-C scenes require `-nc-` infix (G13 fleet-internal carve-out)\n- **G5** Child face detected → full frame rejected (no partial blur)\n- **G6** Byte-determinism — dry-run sha256 == production sha256 (empirically verified, cycle 44)\n- **G7** NVIDIA PhysX NEVER → `kami-genesis` only\n- **G8** OptiX / RTX Renderer / Replicator NEVER → `kami-pbrt` + Embree only\n- **G9** Murakumo-only inference, no commercial GPU rental\n- **G11** PSNR/SSIM/Chamfer/IoU composite ≥ 0.75 quality gate\n- **G12** R1 ≤ 1 GPU-hr-eq/actor/day Murakumo cap\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] e7m-dataset pytest — 251 tests, all green\n- [x] e7m-sim pytest — 122 tests, all green\n- [x] verifier + preflight unit tests — 17 tests, all green\n- [x] **Cumulative**: 390 tests green\n- [x] End-to-end runbook smoke (10/10 documented operator commands work) — cycle 44 evidence at `90-docs/baien/adr-2605262500-runbook-smoke-260527.edn`\n- [x] G6 determinism empirically verified (dry-run sha256 = production sha256 = `c76f6c7fb402…`)\n- [x] deps.toml audit — 41/41 ADR-2605262500 entries clean\n- [ ] GitHub Actions `deps-toml-paths.yml` workflow live-trigger smoke (deferred, will exercise on this PR's first push)\n\n## Operator runbook\n\nSee `90-docs/baien/adr-2605262500-operator-runbook-260527.edn`. Quick start:\n\n```bash\npython3 70-tools/scripts/diagnose/e7m_preflight.py --filter ADR-2605262500\n# → exit 0 = ready; exit 1 = printed operator action items\n```\n\n## Non-goals (preserved from ADR-2605262500)\n\n- **N1** NOT frontier-beating vs Isaac Sim — engineering-investment-bounded\n- **N2** NOT auto-deploying to public PDS — operator-gated\n- **N3** Vision PII filter NOT a guarantee — operator-side jurisdiction policy applies\n- **N4** Tier-C derived recordings MUST NOT publish externally\n- **N5** Not a full Isaac Sim replacement — `e7m-sim` is OSS reference impl\n\n## Dependencies on un-ratified ADRs\n\nNone — ADR-2605262500 stands alone. Sibling ADR-2605262400 (organism\nperception axis) is independent; both can ship in either order.\n\n## What this PR does NOT change\n\n- No changes to Murakumo fleet inference paths (still Murakumo-only)\n- No new commercial GPU rental (continues §2(i) train-only carve-out\n  pending Council ratification per ADR-2605262200)\n- No new external network egress at religious-corp infra\n- No changes to L1 / L2 substrate (Lexicons / contracts unchanged in core)\n\n## Documentation\n\n- ADR canonical: `90-docs/adr/2605262500-robotics-world-data-ingestion-and-usd-pipeline.edn`\n- Implementation retrospective (39-cycle chronology + 5 reusable patterns): `90-docs/baien/adr-2605262500-implementation-retrospective-260527.edn`\n- Operator runbook (production fetch → assemble → eval): `90-docs/baien/adr-2605262500-operator-runbook-260527.edn`\n- Runbook smoke evidence (cycle 44): `90-docs/baien/adr-2605262500-runbook-smoke-260527.edn`\n- CLAUDE.md row #71: operating-time summary\n\n## Co-Authored-By\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n```\n\n---\n\n## Sign-off checklist (operator-side before opening PR)\n\n- [ ] Pick Option A / B / C from Part 1\n- [ ] Run deps.toml drift cleanup PR (Part 2) FIRST as a separate PR\n- [ ] Verify `verify_deps_toml_paths.py` exits 0 on full repo after cleanup\n- [ ] Open ADR-2605262500 PR using draft from Part 3\n- [ ] CI `deps-toml-paths.yml` should pass on PR push\n- [ ] Reviewer ask: focus on ADR-2605262500 §Gates G2/G5/G7/G8/G11 substantive correctness, not 44-cycle minor commit history\n\n## Why this prep doc is separate from the ADR\n\nThe ADR itself is the **decision record**; this doc is the **shipping\npreflight** for that decision's first production PR. Future ADRs on\nthe same topic (R1 / R2) won't need a fresh PR-prep doc unless the\nbranch state is similarly tangled.\n\n## References\n\n- ADR-2605262500 canonical\n- Cycle 39 retrospective (39-cycle chronology)\n- Cycle 42 operator runbook\n- Cycle 44 runbook smoke (Expected vs Observed matrix)\n- This doc (cycle 45)\n", :doc/path "90-docs/baien/adr-2605262500-pr-prep-260527.edn", :doc/source-repo "root", :doc/topic "adr-2605262500-pr-prep", :doc/last_verified "2026-05-27", :doc/date "2026-05-27", :doc/authoritative false, :doc/related ["doc-adr-2605262500-implementation-retrospective-260527" "doc-adr-2605262500-operator-runbook-260527" "doc-adr-2605262500-runbook-smoke-260527" "adr-2605262500-robotics-world-data-ingestion-and-usd-pipeline"], :doc/authoritative_for ["PR scope decision input for ADR-2605262500" "cross-ADR drift owner outreach checklist" "reviewer-facing PR description template"]}]
